WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.043
Phase 1, Foundation, opens
by generating the eight

2
00:00:03.043 --> 00:00:06.475
plans from the committed
assessment and approving them.

3
00:00:06.475 --> 00:00:12.135
It then designs every surface from
those plans, attributes, dynamic groups,

4
00:00:12.135 --> 00:00:15.970
Intune policy, Conditional
Access, sync, DNS and PKI,

5
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:19.713
and builds the shared
foundation the pilot needs.

6
00:00:19.713 --> 00:00:22.962
Group processing is planned
in hours, not minutes.

7
00:00:22.962 --> 00:00:26.849
The steward clears G1 when the
plans and designs are approved,

8
00:00:26.849 --> 00:00:31.878
the baseline Conditional Access policies
are enforced after at least a week in

9
00:00:31.878 --> 00:00:36.070
report-only, the emergency access
accounts are vaulted and tested,

10
00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:39.575
the HR feed is live, and every
High finding is remediated.

11
00:00:39.575 --> 00:00:42.350
Phase 2 proves the whole
pattern on real people.

12
00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:47.551
Book 01 sets the pilot's scope as one
division, typically IT, which tolerates

13
00:00:47.551 --> 00:00:53.088
disruption best, and the master plan's
sizes are a floor for what it must exercise.

14
00:00:53.088 --> 00:00:58.012
It's measured against eight criteria,
from sign-in success to help desk volume.

15
00:00:58.012 --> 00:01:02.933
The values are illustrative: set them in
the decision log before the pilot opens,

16
00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:06.138
and evaluate them from the
systems, not from opinion.

17
00:01:06.138 --> 00:01:09.538
Every surface has a rollback
trigger and a procedure.

18
00:01:09.538 --> 00:01:15.045
G2 is signed jointly by the steward and
the executive sponsor: zero drift for the

19
00:01:15.045 --> 00:01:20.690
agreed hold period, every criterion met,
and no hybrid-joined PC without a cut date.
